From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 03:31:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: nf_flow_table: do not re-add hw offload after teardown

flow_offload_refresh() can queue a FLOW_CLS_REPLACE work that runs
after teardown already destroyed the flow's driver entries. The late
replace re-installs them with nobody left to remove them: they keep
forwarding for a dead conntrack and block offload of any later flow
that reuses the same cookie address.

Skip the refresh re-add once a flow is in teardown, and bail out of
flow_offload_work_add() if NF_FLOW_TEARDOWN is set.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c    |    3 ++-
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c |    8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
@@ -426,7 +426,8 @@ void flow_offload_refresh(struct nf_flow
 		return;
 
 	if (likely(!nf_flowtable_hw_offload(flow_table)) ||
-	    test_bit(NF_FLOW_CLOSING, &flow->flags))
+	    test_bit(NF_FLOW_CLOSING, &flow->flags) ||
+	    test_bit(NF_FLOW_TEARDOWN, &flow->flags))
 		return;
 
 	nf_flow_offload_add(flow_table, flow);
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -978,6 +978,14 @@ static void flow_offload_work_add(struct
 	struct nf_flow_rule *flow_rule[FLOW_OFFLOAD_DIR_MAX];
 	int err;
 
+	/* A queued add can run after teardown already destroyed the
+	 * driver entries; installing here would orphan them as no
+	 * destroy follows. flow->flags is modified with fully ordered
+	 * atomics so a completed destroy implies this flag is visible.
+	 */
+	if (test_bit(NF_FLOW_TEARDOWN, &offload->flow->flags))
+		return;
+
 	err = nf_flow_offload_alloc(offload, flow_rule);
 	if (err < 0)
 		return;
